{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789926925,"nonce":"UY0HTSTffPMDyXaU3bgcd2Sm1O8=","title":"SSA: a comparison against null was emitted before its operand's control flow","message":"translate_null_comparison translated its operand with translate_expression and appended the compare to the block the expression started in. An operand that builds control flow of its own (a conditional value: the Lua frontend's nil-or-table coercion) leaves control in a merge block, so the compare landed before the branch and read the merge's phi: the interpreter saw an undefined register (\"expected integer, got Undef\"). Fixed with translate_operand and settle, as the other binary paths do.","files":null}]}